            "created_at": "2025-09-25T15:43:53.792513+00:00",
            "notes": "Round one you'll want to focus on playing with your team and not being too aggressive just yet.\n\nFor the first power, we will take [Smashing!](item_a7021e28-cb8a-4f39-aeb1-380525b3fea9). This power compliments the playstyle of the first couple rounds nicely, as it boosts [Move Speed](stat_move_speed) and [Weapon Lifesteal](stat_weapon_lifesteal).\n\n [Plasma Converter](item_25869f9a-9a29-4e19-96b6-9d8a28c59318) and [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) combo nicely for early game sustain, and we'll take [Heartbeat Sensor](item_2a4ffaf4-f14b-47d2-a267-0a0e83e87418) for the extra [Move Speed](stat_move_speed); helping to close gaps and secure kills.\n\nAgain, focus mostly on playing with your team and staying alive.\n\n---\n\n**USEFUL INFO:**\n\nAn [Ana](hero_f1aee6cf-704f-455f-a100-ec882ebbe000) can be pretty annoying to play against if she consistently lands her Biotic Grenades and/or Sleep Darts, so I will give advice on how to deal with that on the next round's notes.\n\nA [Mei](hero_36fd67f0-19df-4c50-add9-709cfb147cb0) going for a snowball build can also be very annoying to go against, as they can just push you back when you try to get aggressive, or wall you off from the rest of your team when you push in. If the enemy team is running a snowball build [Mei](hero_36fd67f0-19df-4c50-add9-709cfb147cb0), I recommend playing a bit more opportunistically; playing around her snowball's cooldown.",
